WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.720
Hello everyone!
Let me ask you a question.&nbsp;

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.240
When you look at a price chart,&nbsp;
what do you actually see?&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.120
Most traders see candles going up and down.&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.760
They see patterns.
They see lines.&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.800
But they're missing the most important&nbsp;
piece of information on the entire chart.&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.480
Volume.
Price is just the advertisement.&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.400
Volume is the actual transaction.
It's like judging a restaurant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.680
only by its sign outside, without ever&nbsp;
checking if there are any customers inside.&nbsp;

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.840
In this video, I'm going to show&nbsp;
you how to read volume correctly.&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.880
Not just what volume is.
But what it MEANS.&nbsp;

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.360
Why it matters.
And how to use it to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:44.400
what's really happening behind every move.
After this video, every candle on your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.400
chart will tell you a story.
And volume will be the proof.&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.440
Not financial advice.
Just education.&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.480
Let's get into it.
Let's start with the basics.&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:00.080
Every chart speaks two languages at the same time.
Language number one: Price.&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.280
Price tells you WHAT happened.
Did the market go up?&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.800
Down?
Sideways?&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.880
That's the headline.
The news title.&nbsp;

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.200
Language number two: Volume.
Volume tells you HOW MUCH&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.520
conviction was behind that move.
How many traders participated?&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.880
How much money actually moved there?
That's the evidence.&nbsp;

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.760
The proof.
Think of it like an election.&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.840
Price is the result — who won.
But volume is the number of voters who showed up.&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.240
If only 10 people voted, does&nbsp;
the result really mean anything?&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.920
But if 10 million people&nbsp;
voted — that's a declaration.&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:40.240
Same with the market.
A big green candle on low volume?&nbsp;

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:44.240
Suspicious.
A big green candle on high volume?&nbsp;

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.640
That's conviction.
That's real.&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:52.240
From now on, every time you look at a&nbsp;
chart, don't just ask: "Where did price go?"&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:58.240
Also ask: "How much money stood behind that move?"
Now here's the single most important idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.920
in this entire video.
To read volume correctly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.600
you only need ONE mental model.
Just one.&nbsp;

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.120
Effort versus Result.
In the market:&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.840
Effort is volume — how much energy,&nbsp;
how much money is being used.&nbsp;

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.600
Result is the candle — how&nbsp;
far price actually moved.&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.240
Think of it like pushing a car up a hill.
Your foot on the gas pedal is the effort.&nbsp;

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:27.280
How far the car moves is the result.
Case number one: You press the gas.&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.680
The car moves easily.
Big effort.&nbsp;

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.160
Big result.
Everything matches.&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.000
On the chart, that's a big candle&nbsp;
with high volume underneath.&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.480
Lots of buyers.
Lots of conviction.&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.560
The move is real.
Like a whole stadium standing up to cheer.&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.120
That's genuine excitement.
Case number two: You slam the gas pedal.&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.040
The engine roars.
Fuel is burning.&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.640
But the car barely moves.
There's something blocking the road.&nbsp;

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.880
On the chart, that's a tiny candle&nbsp;
with MASSIVE volume underneath.&nbsp;

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.920
This is called Absorption.
What's happening?&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.040
Buyers are pushing hard, but&nbsp;
there's an invisible wall.&nbsp;

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:09.200
A large seller — smart money — is sitting&nbsp;
there, quietly absorbing every single buy order.&nbsp;

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.440
Think of a dam.
The water keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:17.360
pouring in, but the dam holds everything back.
When the water runs out — when buyers exhaust&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:23.920
themselves — there's nobody left to push price up.
And very often, price drops sharply.&nbsp;

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:30.640
Case number three: You barely touch the gas.
But the car keeps rolling uphill by itself.&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.920
There's no resistance.
The road is empty.&nbsp;

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.840
On the chart, that's price&nbsp;
moving up on LOW volume.&nbsp;

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.240
This is called No Supply.
It doesn't mean buyers are super strong.&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.840
It means sellers are ABSENT.
Nobody is selling.&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.480
So the market doesn't need much effort to move.
Like walking on an empty road.&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.800
No one is blocking your path.
Now here's your cheat sheet.&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:00.160
The Volume Matrix.
High volume plus big candle — healthy move.&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.200
High volume plus small candle — absorption.
Warning sign.&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.160
Low volume plus price still&nbsp;
moving — no supply or no demand.&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.520
The other side is absent.
Memorize these three combinations.&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.400
They're the foundation of&nbsp;
everything that comes next.&nbsp;

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.960
Now let's apply Effort vs Result&nbsp;
to specific candle patterns.&nbsp;

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:27.760
This is Volume Spread Analysis — VSA.
Three patterns every trader should recognize.&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.720
Pattern one: Stopping Volume.
Imagine price is crashing.&nbsp;

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:37.680
Red candle after red candle.
Everyone is panicking and selling.&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:43.520
Then you see this: a tall red candle,&nbsp;
the volume bar underneath is HUGE — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.400
biggest in weeks.
But here's the thing.&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:52.240
The candle doesn't close at the very bottom.
It has a long wick below, and the close is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.400
near the middle.
What happened?&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:59.360
Someone with deep pockets bought EVERYTHING&nbsp;
the panicking sellers were throwing away.&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.440
They didn't stop the crash with words.
They stopped it with money.&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.920
High effort.
Small result.&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.960
The price didn't go lower despite massive volume.
That's absorption at the bottom.&nbsp;

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:16.160
A potential reversal zone.
Pattern two: Buying Climax.&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.920
Now imagine the opposite.
Price has been going up for weeks.&nbsp;

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.640
News is great.
Everyone is bullish.&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.240
Retail traders are jumping in&nbsp;
because they don't want to miss out.&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:31.040
Then you see: a huge green candle.
Volume is EXTREME — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:37.200
highest on the entire chart.
To most traders, this looks like massive strength.&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.280
But here's the plot twist.
This is NOT strong buying.&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:47.360
This is strong selling DISGUISED as buying.
Smart money uses that wall of buy orders from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:53.520
retail traders to unload their massive positions.
They're selling INTO the demand, quietly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.280
without crashing the price.
Like a vendor at a night market.&nbsp;

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.600
The busiest moment?
That's when they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.160
clearing out the last of their stock.
The moment you FOMO in at the top?&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.480
That might be exactly when smart&nbsp;
money is walking out the door.&nbsp;

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:14.000
Pattern three: No Supply Test.
After an uptrend, price pulls back a little.&nbsp;

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.960
You're worried.
"Is this a correction?"&nbsp;

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:21.920
Then you look at volume: a small&nbsp;
red candle, and volume is VERY low.&nbsp;

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:25.600
The market is asking a question:&nbsp;
"Does anyone want to sell here?"&nbsp;

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:31.280
And low volume answers: "No. Not really."
That's a No Supply test.&nbsp;

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:35.360
Sellers are absent.
The uptrend is likely to continue.&nbsp;

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:40.000
Like testing if the fire is hot.
You put your hand near it — it's cool.&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.720
Safe to move forward.
Three patterns.&nbsp;

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:46.480
One mental model.
Effort versus Result.&nbsp;

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.280
That's enough to read eighty percent of&nbsp;
what volume is telling you on any chart.&nbsp;

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:55.920
Now, before we go further, let me clear up&nbsp;
the most common mistake in volume reading.&nbsp;

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.480
And if you've been making&nbsp;
this mistake, don't worry.&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.160
Almost everyone does.
The myth: "Green volume bar means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:07.200
buying. Red volume bar means selling."
That is NOT how it works.&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.920
Here's the truth.
Every single trade requires a buyer AND a seller.&nbsp;

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:13.680
Always.
Without exception.&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:18.080
If you bought 100 shares, someone&nbsp;
else SOLD you those 100 shares.&nbsp;

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.320
Volume counts the NUMBER of transactions.
Not which "side" is winning.&nbsp;

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.160
The color of the volume bar?
It simply follows the color of the candle.&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.440
If the candle closed higher&nbsp;
than it opened — green bar.&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.400
If it closed lower — red bar.
That's it.&nbsp;

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.520
It has nothing to do with who&nbsp;
is buying or who is selling.&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.080
Think of a busy fish market&nbsp;
at five in the morning.&nbsp;

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:42.160
The market is packed — high volume.
But there are buyers AND sellers everywhere.&nbsp;

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:45.600
You can't say "today is all buying"&nbsp;
just because the market is busy.&nbsp;

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.240
Busy means activity.
To know who is WINNING,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:51.680
you look at where the candle closes.
So here's the rule:&nbsp;

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:56.640
Don't look at the COLOR of the volume bar.
Look at the SIZE of the volume bar, combined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:00.800
with where the candle closes.
Size plus close position.&nbsp;

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:05.040
That's where the real story is.
Now let's talk about one of the most powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.200
warning signals in volume analysis.
Volume Divergence.&nbsp;

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:13.280
When price and volume agree with&nbsp;
each other, the trend is healthy.&nbsp;

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.400
Price going up?
Volume going up?&nbsp;

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.280
Strong.
Price going down?&nbsp;

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.800
Volume going down?
The selling is weakening.&nbsp;

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.280
But when price and volume DISAGREE&nbsp;
— that's your early warning system.&nbsp;

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:32.560
Here's the most important one.
Imagine price is making new highs.&nbsp;

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.560
The chart looks great.
Everyone is celebrating.&nbsp;

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.160
But if you look at the volume&nbsp;
bars, they're getting SMALLER.&nbsp;

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:44.080
Each new high has LESS&nbsp;
volume than the previous one.&nbsp;

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.920
Think of a rocket.
At launch, the fuel is full.&nbsp;

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:54.240
The rocket blasts off with enormous power.
But as the fuel burns, the thrust weakens.&nbsp;

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:58.720
The rocket slows down.
And eventually... it falls.&nbsp;

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.840
That's what declining volume&nbsp;
during an uptrend looks like.&nbsp;

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:06.800
The move is running out of fuel.
Fewer and fewer traders believe in the move.&nbsp;

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:11.120
The same works in reverse.
If price is falling but volume keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:17.120
dropping too — sellers are getting exhausted.
Each drop has less and less participation.&nbsp;

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:21.760
The selling is drying up.
That often signals a bottom is forming.&nbsp;

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:25.200
Volume divergence is your&nbsp;
free early warning system.&nbsp;

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.400
The market hasn't crashed yet.
But it's getting tired.&nbsp;

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.920
It's like the applause getting&nbsp;
quieter after each speech.&nbsp;

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:36.240
The audience is losing interest.
The show is almost over.&nbsp;

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:41.680
When you see price making new highs but&nbsp;
volume making lower highs — pay attention.&nbsp;

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:45.040
Something is about to change.
Now let's turn everything into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.160
a simple process you can use on any&nbsp;
chart, any market, starting today.&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:55.200
I call it the 3-Step Volume Check.
Step one: Zoom Out.&nbsp;

00:09:55.200 --> 00:10:00.320
Before you look at individual candles,&nbsp;
zoom out to the daily or weekly chart.&nbsp;

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.240
Ask yourself: Is volume overall&nbsp;
increasing or decreasing?&nbsp;

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:07.520
Are there any unusual volume spikes recently?&nbsp;

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.640
Think of it like checking the&nbsp;
weather before going outside.&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:14.000
You want to know the climate&nbsp;
before you worry about the rain.&nbsp;

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:19.040
Step two: Zoom In to Key Levels.
Find the important support and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.280
resistance levels on your chart.
Now watch what happens when price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:27.280
approaches those levels.
Apply Effort vs Result.&nbsp;

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:32.880
If price touches resistance and volume SPIKES&nbsp;
but the candle stays small — that's absorption.&nbsp;

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.040
The wall is holding.
Be careful.&nbsp;

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:40.880
If price breaks through resistance with a big&nbsp;
candle AND high volume — that's a real breakout.&nbsp;

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:43.520
Effort matches result.
But if price breaks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:50.640
resistance on LOW volume — be suspicious.
A breakout without conviction is often a trap.&nbsp;

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:56.000
Step three: Wait for Confirmation.
This is where most traders go wrong.&nbsp;

00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:01.040
They see one signal and immediately jump in.
Don't do that.&nbsp;

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:06.640
After a breakout, wait for the next candle.
Does price pull back to the broken level?&nbsp;

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:12.000
If it does, and that pullback happens&nbsp;
on LOW volume — that's a No Supply test.&nbsp;

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.800
The market tested the level and found no sellers.
That's your confirmation.&nbsp;

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.960
Patience for one extra candle can&nbsp;
save you from ten losing trades.&nbsp;

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:25.440
Let me show you how this looks in practice.
Price is approaching resistance.&nbsp;

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:30.240
You zoom out — volume has been steady.
Price touches resistance.&nbsp;

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:34.720
Volume spikes.
But the candle is small with a long upper wick.&nbsp;

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.840
High effort, small result.
Absorption.&nbsp;

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.560
The wall is strong.
You don't buy.&nbsp;

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.640
You wait.
Price drops.&nbsp;

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:45.360
You avoided a trap.
Three steps.&nbsp;

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.160
Zoom out.
Zoom in to key levels.&nbsp;

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.600
Wait for confirmation.
That's your volume playbook.&nbsp;

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.360
Before your next trade, run&nbsp;
through this quick checklist.&nbsp;

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:00.160
One: Is volume increasing or&nbsp;
decreasing compared to recent bars?&nbsp;

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:06.160
Two: Does the effort match the result?
Big volume should mean big candles — if not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.440
someone is absorbing.
Three: Are there any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:15.680
unusual volume spikes near key levels?
Four: Is volume diverging from price?&nbsp;

00:12:15.680 --> 00:12:20.960
New highs on lower volume is a warning.
Five: What does the next candle confirm?&nbsp;

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:24.960
Never act on one candle alone.
When you ask these five questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:27.520
you're no longer guessing.
You're reading the market.&nbsp;

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:31.200
You're seeing the proof behind every move.
Because volume is not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:35.760
another indicator on your chart.
Volume is the truth serum of the market.&nbsp;

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:39.120
Price can be pushed around.
Price can be manipulated.&nbsp;

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.240
But volume shows you where real money&nbsp;
— real commitment — is stepping in.&nbsp;

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:49.600
If this video helped you finally see what's&nbsp;
behind the candles, let me know in the comments.&nbsp;

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:53.520
Which pattern are you going to look for first?
Stopping Volume?&nbsp;

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:56.800
Buying Climax?
Or Volume Divergence?&nbsp;

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.960
Drop a comment.
I read every single one.&nbsp;

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.960
I'll see you in the next video.
Stay disciplined.

